    "keying_balance": {
      "Extraversion": "5 positive / 5 reverse",
      "Agreeableness": "6 positive / 4 reverse",
      "Conscientiousness": "6 positive / 4 reverse",
      "Neuroticism": "8 positive / 2 reverse",
      "Openness": "7 positive / 3 reverse"
    },
    "note": "The original IPIP labels Factor IV as 'Emotional Stability' (positive pole) and Factor V as 'Intellect/Imagination'. Here they are relabeled as 'Neuroticism' and 'Openness' respectively to match standard OCEAN terminology. For Neuroticism, the keying direction is REVERSED relative to the original IPIP source: items that were +keyed for Emotional Stability become reverse-scored for Neuroticism, and vice versa. The asymmetric keying per dimension is authentic to the original IPIP-50 instrument."
  },
